[Music]  for the past several years spacex has  been developing starship a giant new  deep space rocket at the company's test  facility in south texas  starship heading back to the landers  testing of starship prototypes has  resulted in fiery failures  but last year starship completed its  first successful suborbital flight and  landing  now spacex ceo elon musk says 2022 is  the year starship will face its biggest  test yet orbital flight i feel at this  point highly confident that we'll get to  orbit this year however it's possible  that starship's historic first orbital  flight test might take place at the  kennedy space center in florida rather  than at starbase in boca chica texas  that's because flight safety regulators  could end up determining more  environmental reviews are needed for the  texas site an orbital test flight is a  really big milestone you know for  starship or really for any you know  rocket that's going to space  so  why after years of development in texas  could spacex's starship make its most  important flight to date in florida  and what could that switch mean for  spacex's operations going forward  on thursday february 10th spacex ceo  elon musk gave his first update on the  company's starship program in about two  years  towering behind him at the company's  south texas starbase was starship the  essential technology the the holy grail  breakthrough that's needed is a  rapid and completely reusable rocket  system  when stacked on top of its massive  booster called super heavy starship  stands at 120 meters or 400 feet  making it the tallest rocket ever  constructed  starship according to elon musk is meant  to go to mars the starship rocket system  is meant to be a fully reusable  multi-planetary  rocket system  nasa selected starship as the vehicle to  get astronauts to land on the surface of  the moon by 2025  and the pentagon said it wants to use  starship to transport military cargo but  before all that can happen starship  needs to be tested in orbit  spacex has been able to  conduct these shorter  shorter flights no more than 18 miles up  but this year you know elon musk says  he's he's pretty sure that that star  ship is going to go to orbit the orbital  test mission still needs sign off from  the faa which has been conducting an  environmental assessment of the  company's proposal to operate starship  in texas the faa of course is is even  looking at this in the first place  because  the agency monitors and regulates space  launch facilities  launches themselves and then re-entries  last year the faa held hearings about  the starship proposal for the texas  location and received around 19 000  comments on the initiative one of the  questions with the fda's current review  for the proposal for starship in texas  is  are they going to have to do additional  review on environmental grounds you know  beyond that  in 2021 the journal reported the boko  chika residents said the starship  project is damaging to the local  wetlands and wildlife  they move in  and change the whole tone and tenor of  the place but but they began to do 24 7  construction which meant  you know wall-to-wall people cars  traffic noise lighting  uh you name it the agency is considering  you know the potential impact of using  the vehicles at the site  everything from noise to what it would  mean for surrounding  wildlife and wetlands musk said that if  in addition to its current environmental  assessment or ea the faa requires spacex  to conduct a more in-depth eis or  environmental impact statement of the  starbase site spacex would consider  moving its orbital test to the kennedy  space center  in a statement the faa wrote completing  the environmental review does not  guarantee that a vehicle operator  license will be issued to spacex the  environmental review is just one part of  the faa commercial space licensing  process  spacex must also meet faa safety risk  and financial responsibility  requirements it would obviously set us  back  for quite some time because uh  an eis takes a lot longer than  an ea  so we would have to shift our priorities  to cape kennedy spacex already has  permission to use a launch site at the  kennedy space center for starship  in december musk said in a tweet that  spacex had started building an orbital  launch pad for starship at the florida  location the short answer to  if you know is spacex abandoning texas  you know to shift this program to  florida is no it's possible that the  starbase site  could end up as spacex's kind of  long-term  sort of research site r d  whereas the operational  sort of launch pad would be in florida  they know that they're they're good to  go there you know and in terms of like  all environmental reviews and analysis  it's sort of more plug and play whereas  texas you still have this this question  of what the result of the current review  is going to be  and at least the possibility that  there's going to be another  environmental review  you know beyond that the faa said it  planned to release its environmental  review on march 28th we don't have a ton  of insight into  the  where things stand with the faa um  we have gotten sort of a rough  indication that there may be an approval  uh in march  but that's all we know  [Music]  will culminate with landing on the  landing pad in boca chica  [Music]

